{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I.</b> The word מבול (flood): some say the dagesh stands in place of a hidden nun, like מבוע, and it is from the root of \"אבלה נבלה הארץ\" (Isaiah 24:4). Others say it is from בלולה בשמן (mixed with oil), and it should have been on the pattern of מסלול (Isaiah 35:8), and like it המשור (ibid. 10:15 [sic]), and the cholam and the shureq interchange." "And the meaning of המבול מים (the flood of waters) is by way of ellipsis, and likewise it is המבול מבול מים, and likewise \"למן היום הוסדה\" (Exodus 9:18), whose meaning is למן היום יום הוסדה:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites המשור as from Isaiah 10:15 but the word appears in Isaiah 10:15 (המשור מרים את עצמו); rendered 'ibid.' following his שם reference though the chapter cited (10) differs from the previous one (35). The phrase 'בלולה בשמן' is not a biblical citation but a lexical illustration.", 1 "Ibn Ezra's point is that the phrase expands by repetition; translated hyper-literally without adding connective explanation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:36.845808123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}